    "description": "The Gold Beach Tremont tree farm consists of four tracts totaling over 2,700 acres. Well managed stands with varying age classes and a strong merchantable component. 27 separate parcels ofwhich many have had approved CUP's in the past. One current CUP which expires in 2027. Views of the Wedderburn Bridge, Rogue River and Pacific Ocean from multiple vantage points. The Libby Tract, included in the offering, has two wells and a septic system installed. Each tract has gated entries and the roads have recently been brushed and graded. Timber and development related information provided with signed non-disclosure agreement. Buyers to verify all information to own satisfaction.",
